Just to make sure we are on the same page, do you want to use pre-built by Temporal Docker images? You don't need to fork Temporal code to be able to implement a custom Authorizer. Just importing the Temporal library as the dependency will do. Something like this:
```
package main

  import (
      "go.temporal.io/server/temporal"
      "go.temporal.io/server/common/authorization"
      "go.temporal.io/server/common/config"
  )

  func main() {
      cfg, err := config.LoadConfig("development", "", "")
      if err != nil {
          log.Fatal(err)
      }

      s, err := temporal.NewServer(
          temporal.ForServices(temporal.DefaultServices),
          temporal.WithConfig(cfg),
          temporal.WithAuthorizer(NewMyAuthorizer()),
          temporal.WithClaimMapper(func(cfg *config.Config) authorization.ClaimMapper {
              return NewMyClaimMapper()
          }),
      )
  }
```

Wanted to make sure you are aware of this, since you would need to compile the plugin anyways.
